# Build output. ANCHORED on purpose: an unanchored `target/` or `out/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which silently ignores files you meant to track.
/target/
/dist/

# Rust and editor leftovers.
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig
.DS_Store
/.direnv

# Development working notes: the research inputs and the audit reports. Kept locally, never
# published — the durable copy is whatever checkout happens to hold them.
/out/

# The bench harness was removed from the repository on 2026-10-07 (it vendored a corpus of
# other people's workflows and a cargo target/ dir, 899 tracked files). Restore it locally with
# `git checkout d632d43 -- bench`, and this keeps a restore out of the repo.
/bench/
